 kept: {
  as: current,
  why: "ProbeRuns' box matrix on fierce's frozen baseline, export_c804ccb (image 264e7b7c) on kexport_c804ccb (ELF c12d64ac), P0, 1KA1, the factory route, every arm `--host` with JAB_AUDIO none, through jab-stress's gauge_batches runner from 05:32 to 07:09: seventeen batches, 45 runs, every batch ok. The probed batches at cadences 0 1 2 2 1 0 and the oracle's three traced runs read by ProbeRuns' reader at jab-stress 4c0bf6f over jab c804ccb: every pairing admitted on its recorded bounds; 60.2, 55.6, and 58.8 percent of frames shown at cadences 0, 1, and 2, superseded runs of two at most, no repeats, SDL's offscreen renders every 30.0 ms; presented every 16.67 to 16.70 ms; K violations by the thousand at cadences 0 and 1 under P0, as P0's catch-up gives them, and none at cadence 2. The observer set: the shim's effect past its noise on the flip call's median (0.044 ms) and the completion interval's median (0.005 ms), so the probed readings are instrumented-only. The window's cost, offscreen SDL against headless: the flip call 1.147 ms longer at the median and the critical path with it, the drawing and the acceptance intervals unchanged. The readings proberuns.nuon, observer.nuon, and window.nuon kept; the batches' runs, pads, and logs archived; each step's gauge report derived by the batch reread; each disk copy kept as its hash. Cited by the fps subiter's plan/agenda/FrameCeiling/FrameCadence/CadenceGauge/ProbeRuns.md."
 },
